      "body": "Complete — merged via the merge queue as PR #93 (mergedAt 2026-07-23T05:46:46Z).\n\nDoD evidence: (1) Policy table declared as data in src/r4g1.rs: ExactContext → Serve, Graph → Serve, Novel → WidenOnce (retry once at 2xTOP_M) then Abstain, Contradictory → Abstain (arm implemented and unit-asserted); optional config.status_policy override in score_report.json with lenient fallback. (2) API responses include status/widened/abstained: POST /api/r4g1/predict returns {abstained:false,prediction:{status,token,widened}} on serve and HTTP 200 {abstained:true,status:'novel',widened:true} on abstain (repeat: widened:false via widen-once memory); chat abstain is HTTP 200 with generation_mode r4g1-abstained and an explicit r4g1 status block — never a silent fall-through; the pathological guard stays the last line for served output. (3) Probe suite 11/11: OOD → widen → abstain (counters widen_attempts=1, abstains=1), covered → serve (ExactContext/Graph), identical Novel probe → no second widen (widen_skipped_seen=9), 16 repeated probes deterministic, generate mid-abstain stops with status, step↔reference parity at both widths, out-of-vocab typed error (no panic). (4) Contract preserved: the new step layer (score_step + StepState) is integer-only (source-scanned block) and allocation-free — census: 0 allocations/0 bytes across warm-up, predict(serve), predict(abstain), generate(16), and 8 repeated OOD probes; predict_window delegate 0/0. (5) Verified by maintainer agent: 49 suites, clippy -D warnings, fmt clean, κ-reproduction green; PR checks all green; merged through the queue. Live endpoint examples: served {'status':'graph','token':10}, abstained {'status':'novel','widened':true}, real smollm2 bundle serves 'exact_context' per reference.",
